/**
\mainpage GraphMine native runtime

This is the code-level reference for the current native runtime. For plain-language
problem definitions, runnable operations, and research references, return to
<a href="../../problem/taxonomy/">the family guides</a>.

\section entry Entry points

- graphmine::runtime::request accepts one JSON request and returns a JSON response.
- graphmine_runtime_request provides the same protocol through the C ABI.
- graphmine::Graph preserves canonical records and external identities.
- The view types and builders declare graph normalization and memory layout.
- Runtime family implementations compute the catalog's operations.

Use the file and namespace indexes to inspect current definitions and source.
A research-paper repository is not automatically an executable implementation.

\section protocol Request and result contracts

The catalog command returns available families, problems, operation schemas, and
compiled backends. A run request identifies its operation, graph input, parameters,
and device. Failures return a structured error. Check the result's completeness,
quality, provenance, and operation-specific certificates before consuming it.

\fn std::string graphmine::runtime::request(std::string_view json_request)
\brief Execute one native JSON protocol request.
\param json_request JSON describing the command and its inputs.
\return Serialized JSON result, or an object containing a structured error.

\fn int graphmine::runtime::abi_version() noexcept
\brief Return the version of the native request ABI.

\fn int graphmine_runtime_request(const char* request, size_t length, char** response, size_t* response_length)
\brief Execute a JSON request through the versioned C ABI.
\param request Input bytes, which need not be null terminated.
\param length Number of input bytes.
\param response Receives the allocated response bytes.
\param response_length Receives the number of response bytes.
\return Zero when a response was allocated; minus one for invalid output pointers or allocation failure. A zero return still requires inspecting the JSON for an algorithm error.

\fn void graphmine_runtime_free(void* response)
\brief Release memory returned by graphmine_runtime_request.
\param response Allocation returned by the native request function.
*/
